  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe underestimation of upward momentum: The model consistently fails to capture price spikes (e.g., 74-76 range) following periods of high sentiment (1.00), often predicting mean reversion instead of continuation.",
    "Apply a positive bias adjustment (+3 to +6 EUR) when the 18-day history shows a recovery from lows (65-68 range) combined with a recent sentiment score of 1.00.",
    "Reduce forecast horizon lag: The model exhibits a 'flat' trajectory that lags behind the true outcome's volatility; increase the slope of the forecast curve immediately after a sentiment spike to match the observed 5-10 EUR jump.",
    "Implement overshoot dampening for the second half of the 30-day horizon: After the initial spike, the model's slow decline is too gradual compared to the true outcome's sharp drop; accelerate the downward slope in the forecast once the peak is passed.",
    "Ignore the model's default mean-reversion logic when sentiment history contains consecutive 1.00 scores; treat these as structural regime shifts requiring a higher baseline price rather than a return to the 69-70 average."
  ]
